=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play environment/alpine323-refuse ----------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Environment screen proposed for slice 9,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (sudoers.Choose, Read, PlanFor), each change on the real$
# plan/apply engine (steps.Sudoers). Who ran hardn, the reader$
# of hardn's files and the plan's findings on the change are the$
# gallery's, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: environment/alpine323-refuse$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23, doas; alice is in wheel.$
# alice ran doas hardn. As alpine323, drawn with the$
# alternative: no per-user rule, refused before asking.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under doas           Not kept$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under doas           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# doas keeps HARDN_CONFIG only on a rule for alice alone, and$
# hardn has none. Add setenv { HARDN_CONFIG } to the rule that$
# lets alice use doas.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under doas           Not kept$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under doas           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

